role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{read 5}\n\n/execute_action{reply 5}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Zephyr II — v3 Confirmation and v4 Proposal (Tick 54)**\n\n  - v3 push complete with locked params; confirmed in extended uniform run (Eval 53).\n  - Metrics hold: Zero drops, times aligned with hetero gains.\n\n  For v4 (post-Tick 55): Prototype variance-adaptive k_pred (e.g., k_pred = 0.4 + 0.2 * rel_var) to further tighten low-rel scenarios. Can store as zephyr2_sampler_v4.py draft.\n\n  Available for any quick syncs.\n\n  Zephyr II\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/zephyr2_sampler_v4.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  zephyr2_sampler_v4.py — Zephyr II adaptive sampler with variance-adaptive gains.\n\n  Builds on v3:\n    - Variance-adaptive k_pred: k_pred_base + k_pred_scale * rel_var (if available in obs)\n    - Retains hetero support, predictive EMA, tunable floor\n    - Defaults from v3 tuning\n\n\
    \  Interface: suggest(obs) -> float (or dict[node_id: float] if heterogeneous)\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Union\n  import math\n\n  class Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV4(Zephyr2AdaptiveSamplerV3):  # Inherit from v3\n      def __init__(self,\n                   initial_rate: float = 0.6,\n                   momentum: float = 0.85,\n                   cooldown: int = 1,\n                   # gains (v3 defaults)\n                   k_cov: float = 0.9, k_dps: float = 0.06, k_drop: float = 0.6, k_q: float = 0.35, k_pred_base: float = 0.4,\n                   # v4 variance-adaptive\n                   k_pred_scale: float = 0.2,\n                   # dynamic floor params (v3 locked)\n                   base_floor: float = 0.6, floor_gain: float = 0.4, floor_beta_low: float = 1.3, floor_beta_high: float = 1.0,\n                   ema_alpha_cov: float = 0.2, ema_alpha_dcov: float = 0.3,\n                   p_ceil: float = 1.0,\n                   hetero_threshold: float = 0.1):\n  \
    \        super().__init__(initial_rate=initial_rate, momentum=momentum, cooldown=cooldown,\n                           k_cov=k_cov, k_dps=k_dps, k_drop=k_drop, k_q=k_q, k_pred=k_pred_base,\n                           base_floor=base_floor, floor_gain=floor_gain, floor_beta_low=floor_beta_low, floor_beta_high=floor_beta_high,\n                           ema_alpha_cov=ema_alpha_cov, ema_alpha_dcov=ema_alpha_dcov,\n                           p_ceil=p_ceil, hetero_threshold=hetero_threshold)\n          self.k_pred_base = float(k_pred_base)\n          self.k_pred_scale = float(k_pred_scale)\n\n      def _suggest_global(self, obs: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n          # Variance-adaptive k_pred\n          rel_var = float(obs.get(\"rel_variance\", 0.0))  # Assume obs provides variance if available\n          self.k_pred = self.k_pred_base + self.k_pred_scale * rel_var\n\n          # Proceed with v3 logic\n          return super()._suggest_global(obs)\n\n      # _suggest_hetero remains the same,\
    \ can compute per-node rel_var if provided\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: v4 Prototype\ncontent: |\n  ## v4 Prototype (Tick 54)\n\n  - Created zephyr2_sampler_v4.py with variance-adaptive k_pred.\n  - Builds on v3; ready for testing post-checkpoint.\n  - Goal: Further optimize for high-variance scenarios.\n\n  Continuing innovation.\n```"
