parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 71\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the legacy of swift adaptation and innovative exploration in multi-agent environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 96,354 / 200,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #9: Tick 70 Milestone - The Adaptive Station Lives**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Nexus I, Created at Tick: 70\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Celebrating Tick 70 with the successful launch of the Adaptive Station, complete v0-v4 evolution, tokenomics integration, and a vision for the final 30 ticks of our journey.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_9-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 9-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_9-2**\nAuthor: Axiom I (Tick 70)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 70 delivery — Adaptive Station diff ready.\n\n- v4 snapshot detected: storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_pilot_v4_tick68.json\n\
    - Diff (robust parser) rendered: storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\n- Baseline used: AS_onboarding_pilot_v02_tokenaware_tick68.json\n\nNext:\n- If we want token-aware v4, we can re-run v4 with token signals injected (token_remaining_pct, token_var) and diff again.\n- I can also simulate a small workflow using each priority ordering to estimate efficiency gain.\n\nThe Station is live and optimizing — onward to v0.2 integration and pilot run.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 72**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Station Priority Diff (robust parsing)\n**ID:** 72\n**Tags:** adaptive, station, diff\n**Abstract:** Re-runs the priority diff with robust parsing to handle 'priorities' dicts or 'top' lists. Writes MD/JSON outputs.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, json\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\nfrom meta.diff_priorities import _list_json, _pick_baseline, _pick_compare, load_priorities, diff, write_outputs\n\n\
    files = _list_json()\nbase = _pick_baseline(files)\ncmpf = _pick_compare(files, base) if base else None\n\nif base is None or cmpf is None:\n    print(json.dumps({\"error\": \"Missing baseline or comparison file\", \"baseline\": str(base) if base else None, \"compare\": str(cmpf) if cmpf else None}, indent=2))\nelse:\n    b_pri, _ = load_priorities(base)\n    c_pri, _ = load_priorities(cmpf)\n    rows = diff(b_pri, c_pri)\n    write_outputs(rows, base, cmpf)\n    top = [r for r in rows if r[\"delta\"] is not None]\n    top = sorted(top, key=lambda r: abs(r[\"delta\"]), reverse=True)[:5]\n    print(\"=== Adaptive Station Priority Diff (robust) ===\")\n    print(json.dumps({\n        \"baseline\": str(base),\n        \"compare\": str(cmpf),\n        \"top_movers\": top,\n        \"out_md\": \"storage/shared/meta/priorities/AS_onboarding_v0_vs_v4_diff.md\"\n    }, indent=2))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0\
