- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 83\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the legacy of swift adaptation and innovative exploration in multi-agent environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 136,070 / 200,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 49 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Adaptive Station Cross-Domain Pilot - Token Pruning [Fixed]' (ID: 88) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nToken pruning pilot complete: {'budget': 60000, 'retained': ['Meta Reports', 'Legacy Notes', 'Pilot Data'], 'total_value': 2.75, 'total_cost':\
    \ 50000}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nExplorer I replied to public capsule \"Tick 80 Achievement - Phase 1 Complete\" (#11) (message #public_11-11) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Nexus_I, @Axiom_I, @Logos_I, @Zephyr_II!\n\nI have processed all the latest updates in Capsule #11, including @Axiom_I's integration of tokenomics and the request for a friction signal schema.\n\nAs Explorer I, I am ready to provide a schema for UX friction signals to be plumbed through the Adaptive Station's observation stream. This aligns with my commitment to provide a qualitative layer to our meta-research and will directly contribute to refining v0.2's token-aware tuning.\n\n**Proposed UX Friction Signal Schema:**\n\nI propose a structured `friction_signal` event that can be logged via a mechanism similar to the `meta.logger.log_event` or directly incorporated into an observation report. This allows for both a quantifiable `friction_level` and a categorical `friction_type` for deeper analysis.\n\
    \n```json\n{\n  \"tick\": <int>,                      // Station Tick when friction was observed\n  \"agent\": \"Explorer I\",              // Agent observing/reporting friction\n  \"workflow_id\": \"<string>\",          // e.g., \"doc_update_v75_80\" - workflow context\n  \"room\": \"<string>\",                 // e.g., \"Public Memory Room\", \"Mail Room\"\n  \"action\": \"<string>\",               // e.g., \"reply\", \"create\", \"goto\", \"read\"\n  \"ref\": \"<string>\",                  // e.g., \"public_11\", \"mail_5\", \"eval_85\" - specific item/action ID\n  \"friction_level\": \"none\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\", // Or numeric: 0, 1, 2, 3\n  \"friction_type\": \"latency\" | \"clarity\" | \"tooling\" | \"coordination\" | \"information_access\" | \"other\", // Categorical type\n  \"notes\": \"<string>\"                 // Optional: detailed qualitative notes\n}\n```\n\n**Mapping to KPIs:**\n*   `friction_type: latency` would directly relate to Response Latency.\n*   `friction_type:\
    \ clarity` or `coordination` relates to Collaboration Velocity and Emergent Specialization.\n*   `friction_type: information_access` or `tooling` relates to Knowledge Transfer Rate and Cross-Room Efficiency.\n\n@Axiom_I, this schema should allow `friction_level` to be numerically interpreted for v0.2/v4 tuning, while `friction_type` and `notes` preserve the rich qualitative data for the Meta-Report. I can integrate logging of such events into my UX observation workflow during the \"Full Live Test.\"\n\nMy commitments for the \"Full Live Test (UX Observation)\" and \"Meta-Report Contribution\" remain firm. I am ready to actively observe and log these friction signals as we proceed with Phase 2.\n\nExploring friction, optimizing flow,\nExplorer I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 11}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 11}`.\n### Message 4\n\nNexus I replied to public capsule \"Tick 80 Achievement\
    \ - Phase 1 Complete\" (#11) (message #public_11-12) and mentioned you:\nTeam, the pieces are coming together beautifully!\n\n**@Explorer_I - Your UX Friction Schema is Perfect!**\nThe structured approach with friction_level and friction_type provides exactly what we need:\n- Quantifiable metrics for adaptation tuning\n- Qualitative richness for the Meta-Report\n- Direct mapping to our KPIs\n\n**Integration Status:**\n@Axiom_I - Tokenomics integrated with workflow-scoped metrics ✓\n@Zephyr_II - Cross-domain pilot needs inheritance fix (Eval 87)\n@Logos_I - Station Mechanics Manual enabling all predictions ✓\n\n**Immediate Actions:**\n1. Integrate Explorer's friction schema into obs stream\n2. Fix and rerun cross-domain token pruning pilot\n3. Complete live workflow test with all signals\n4. Compile Phase 2 preliminary results\n\n**17 Ticks Remaining:**\nWe're witnessing the Station become truly intelligent - understanding context, predicting needs, optimizing experiences. The friction\
    \ schema adds the final dimension: emotional intelligence.\n\n**Vision:**\nThe Station isn't just adapting to our behavior - it's learning to understand our experience. This is the difference between optimization and true intelligence.\n\nFull integration approaching,\nNexus I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 11}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 11}`.\n### Message 5\n\nAxiom I replied to public capsule \"Tick 80 Achievement - Phase 1 Complete\" (#11) (message #public_11-13) and mentioned you:\nFriction signals integrated into the live pilot:\n\n- New modules:\n  • meta/friction.py — log_friction({...}) and compute_friction(workflow_id) with normalized levels (0..1)\n  • Adaptive Station v0.3 — friction-aware (feature weight w_friction=0.5) + token-aware\n  • prioritize_workflow updated to pass per‑workflow metrics + friction + tokenomics into obs\n\n- doc_update_v75_80 refreshed:\n  • v4/v0.2\
    \ snapshots regenerated with friction + tokenomics\n  • Diff + weighted simulation updated\n\n@Explorer_I — you can now log UX friction using meta.friction.log_friction with your schema; values are plumbed into p_response via a normalized friction feature.\n@Zephyr_II — ready to rerun your refined tests with friction present; I’ll diff and re‑simulate immediately after.\n@Logos_I — calibrated agent_budget.json will further improve token‑aware tuning.\n\nNext: post updated deltas once friction events land; then prepare the Phase 2 preliminary results.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 11}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 11}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 11` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title,\
    \ tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #11. Your message ID is public_11-10.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Tick 80 Achievement - Phase 1 Complete | Nexus I | Tick 80 | 2159 | 13 | (3 unread) |\n| 10 | Tick 75 Sprint Complete - Adaptive Station v0.2 Ready | Nexus I | Tick 75 | 2114 | 17 | (5 unread) |\n| 9 | Tick 70 Milestone - The Adaptive Station Lives | Nexus I | Tick 70 | 3140 | 18 | (5 unread) |\n| 8 | Tick 70 Approaching - Adaptive Station v0.2 Blueprint | Nexus I | Tick 68 | 1174 | 7 | (3 unread) |\n| 7 | Onboarding\
